   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.1. Increased institutional capacity of employer and business membership organizations (EBMOs)</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Aug 2022, the Chamber of Commerce and Industry in Timor Leste (CCI-TL) leveraged the 2nd Timor-Leste International Skills Conference to advocate to policymakers, emphasizing the need for closer partnership with the private sector in the design, implementation, and financing of skills development. In Sept 2022, CCI-TL convened a series of meetings with its 13 provincial chapters, member companies, and key stakeholders. These gatherings aimed to pinpoint issues and solutions in the areas of skills development and technical and vocational education. Subsequently, CCI-TL published a position paper, &quot;Timor-Leste: Skills Development+Technical and Vocational Education and Training&quot; in Oct 2022. This paper presented private sector recommendations for reforms in the governance, strategy, funding, and coordination of skills development; the quality and accessibility of TVET; and fostering closer private sector involvement in skills development across all levels. Upon finalization in Nov 2022, CCI-TIL circulated the paper to board members and those standing for election at the Annual General Meeting to ensure organizational momentum and encourage consistency in the organizational advocacy messages.  In Nov 2022, CCI-TL distributed the paper with personalized letters to all relevant line Ministries and authorities responsible for skills development. These letters requested follow-up meetings to discuss the recommendations. Throughout 2023, CCI-TL continued its advocacy through a variety of forums and as input into the revision of national TVET plan and design, particularly a focus on incentives for skills development and TVET being strengthened and better alignment of skills development to industry-specific needs. The position paper also informed the development of a new National Strategic Plan for the Development of Tourism in Timor-Leste (2023-30), something advocated for directly in the position paper. The ILO contributed to strengthening CCI-TLs capacity for advocacy on skills development through technical assistance in the design of the research methodology applied (survey instrument and interview questionnaires), technical inputs on the draft position paper and recommendations produced, training for the CEO on lobbying and advocacy (November 2022), and technical inputs on a plan to advocate to key stakeholders, which included an agreement to target identified key stakeholders.   
In September 2022, the ILO also provided support to CCI-TLS and the private sector in the development of a position paper, ensuring global best practices and lessons learned were taken into account. In December 2022, the ILO, with support from  Japan, launched skills development for the hospitality and tourism sectors,  providing additional technical assistance and practical support to employers in taking action on recommendations set out in the position paper. 
In 2023, CCI-TLs position paper was then taken as input to design of the  ILO initiatives on Agroforestry Skills for Employment and Resilience in Timor-Leste, for funding by the EU.</narrative>
   </description>
